    "['switchport trunk allowed vlan [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members [100 200]', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members [100 200]\\n##\\n\\nFor interface GigabitEthernet1/0/2, you would use:\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/2 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members [100 200]\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you need to configure this for each interface separately, and the interface naming convention uses \"ge\" instead of \"GigabitEthernet\". The \"unit 0 family ethernet-switching\" is required for switchport interfaces in Juniper.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members [100 200]'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/2 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members [100 200]', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members [100 200]\\n##\\n\\nFor interface GigabitEthernet1/0/2, you would use:\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/2 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members [100 200]\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you need to configure this for each interface separately, and the interface naming convention uses \"ge\" instead of \"GigabitEthernet\". The \"unit 0 family ethernet-switching\" is required for switchport interfaces in Juniper.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/2 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members [100 200]'}]]": 1
